  m_Name: GwenQuill
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ResumeData
  applicantName: Gwen Quill
  body: '<b>GWEN QUILL</b>

    Applying for: Social Media Manager


    <b>EXPERIENCE</b>

    Social
    Media Manager - Crumb & Co. Bakery

    {dates}

    Grew the bakery''s account
    from {growth}

    {viral}


    <b>SKILLS</b>

    {skill_writing}, photography


    <b>REFERENCES</b>

    {ref}'
  claims:
  - id: dates
    text: Apr 2022 - Present
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 1
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Why leave the bakery?
      answer: I love it, but I can't make the croissants {b_famous}. I need a bigger
        challenge.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: b_famous
        text: any more famous
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: There's a croissant with its own fan club. I'm not joking.
          It has a newsletter.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: Four years at the bakery!
      answer: Four years. I've gained four pounds. Totally worth it.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: growth
    text: 200 to 40,000 followers
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 0
    designerNote: True, and she proves it. A good mark here is correct.
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: 200 to 40,000 followers. Can you prove it?
      answer: Sure! I have the {g_graph} on my phone. Most of the growth came from
        {g_dog}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: g_graph
        text: monthly analytics
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Here. See the big spike? That's the dog.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
      - id: g_dog
        text: the baker's dog
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: His name is Muffin. He wears a tiny chef hat. The internet
          lost its mind.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: 40,000 followers is great growth.
      answer: Thank you! All real people. Mostly grandmas. Grandmas love bread.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: viral
    text: 'Viral post: ''Croissant or Cat?'' (2.1M views)'
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 0
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: '''Croissant or Cat?'' really got 2.1 million views?'
      answer: It did! Photos of croissants and cats that look the same. Some of them
        {c_hard}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: c_hard
        text: were genuinely hard to tell apart
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: There's one we still aren't sure about. We don't talk about
          it.
        callOutDemeanor: 2
    goodQuestion:
      question: I love 'Croissant or Cat?'.
      answer: Thank you! The sequel is 'Bagel or Dog'. It's in development.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: skill_writing
    text: Copywriting
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 4
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Is your writing actually any good?
      answer: 'I {w_wrote} on our bags: ''Butter believe it.'''
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: w_wrote
        text: wrote the slogan
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Sales went up 20%. People love a pun.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: A good writer! Rare.
      answer: I also write a newsletter called 'Knead to Know'. I'm sorry. I can't
        stop.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: ref
    text: Rosa Crumb, owner of Crumb & Co.
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 5
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Is Rosa Crumb a real person?
      answer: Very real. She {r_bread} if you call her.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: r_bread
        text: will try to sell you bread
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: She can't help it. She sold bread to a mailman every day
          for 15 years.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: Will Rosa speak well of you?
      answer: She cried when I said I was leaving. Then she gave me a cake. Then
        she cried again.
      demeanor: 2
      phrases: []
  referenceLetter: 'To whom it may concern,


    Gwen {rl_grew} our bakery''s following
    and {rl_cake}. She posts with care.


    Would I hire her again? In a heartbeat.
    Come by and try the sourdough.


    Rosa Crumb

    Crumb & Co. Bakery'
